<title>SRI LANKA: Kotagala sharply up on growth prospects.</title>
<headline>Kotagala sharply up on growth prospects.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Sri Lanka's Kotagala Plantations Ltd rose 6.67 percent, or 2.25 rupees, to 36 on retail buying in early Wednesday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Retailers are keen on plantation shares because they are expected to see good growth in 1997, and they are cheap,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Plantation shares are seen doing well on continuing demand for Sri Lanka tea from the Commonwealth of Independent States. Kotagala Plantations is one of six privatised estate firms trading in Colombo.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
